# Registers the startup FailureAnalyzer. Do NOT delete this file.
#
# Written in English on purpose: .properties-family files are read as ISO-8859-1
# (java.util.Properties), so UTF-8 Korean turns into mojibake in editors and in
# any tool that reads it as a properties file. Comments are dropped by the parser,
# so it never broke anything -- but a warning nobody can read is not a warning.
#
# Rationale (Korean) lives in StateDirLockFailureAnalyzer's KDoc, which is a .kt
# file and renders fine. Short version: without this registration the lock-conflict
# message gets buried under three layers of bean-creation stack traces, and this
# repository treats the startup log as its diagnostic surface.
#
# This registration is verified by neither the compiler nor the tests. A wrong FQN
# is silently ignored by Spring -- rename the package and you lose the diagnostic
# with no signal. Start two servers on one state dir to check it still fires.
org.springframework.boot.diagnostics.FailureAnalyzer=\
io.wikilens.StateDirLockFailureAnalyzer
